        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> The link you provide clearly states that it is a table based on extension and not filetype (you can read about it in `:h filetype` and `:h 'filetype'`).\r\n\r\nYes, but this table has a key of `lua` [there](https://github.com/nvim-tree/nvim-web-devicons/blob/56f17def81478e406e3a8ec4aa727558e79786f3/lua/nvim-web-devicons/icons-default.lua#L2363), while `mini.icons`'s extension-based table does not have a key for `lua`. Do you mind helping me understand why `mini.icons` does not have such common file extensions included in its `extension_icons` table? @echasnovski \r\n",
