        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Yes, but this table has a key of `lua` [there](https://github.com/nvim-tree/nvim-web-devicons/blob/56f17def81478e406e3a8ec4aa727558e79786f3/lua/nvim-web-devicons/icons-default.lua#L2363), while `mini.icons`'s extension-based table does not have a key for `lua`. Do you mind helping me understand why `mini.icons` does not have such common file extensions included in its `extension_icons` table?\r\n\r\nBecause it [gets resolved via `vim.filetype.match()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a535342b6105a684f16114f598d44318e6a1d20f/doc/mini-icons.txt#L356-L357) removing the need to actually track all possible extensions in 'mini.icons' itself, only all valid filetypes.\r\n\r\nTo be clear, 'mini.icons' very much does have support for '.lua' extension (this is even explicitly [mentioned in help](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a535342b6105a684f16114f598d44318e6a1d20f/doc/mini-icons.txt#L297-L298)). The problem here is that it is not listed in `MiniIcons.list('extension')`, which is mostly a small price to pay for not having to track all possible extensions.\r\n\r\nThere are at least two ways to have 'mini.icons' work with 'barbecue.nvim':\r\n- Make PR to 'barbecue.nvim' to stop using `require('nvim-web-devicons').get_icons()` in favor of a single `require('nvim-web-devicons').get_icon()` (which is already optimized).\r\n- Make PR to 'barbecue.nvim' to have direct support for 'mini.icons': check if `_G.MiniIcons` is present and use `_G.MiniIcons.get('file', ...)` to get icon data.\r\n- Add specific extensions in [`config.extensions`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a535342b6105a684f16114f598d44318e6a1d20f/doc/mini-icons.txt#L195) inside `require('mini.icons').setup()` . Those will be recognized inside `MiniIcons.list()` (and `require('nvim-web-devicons').get_icons()` respectively).",
